            "review_title": "Review at Kouzina - Greek Restaurant",
            "review_text": "journey960\nAustralia67 contributions\n2\nAbsolutely fabulous!!\nFeb 2020 • Solo\nFrom the moment you enter this gem of more than a restaurant you feel an amazing sense of freedom the essence of Greek hospitality.\nThere has been thought and effort to design and create an indoor /outdoor feeling as the floors resemble coblestone alleys on Greek Cyclades island.Blue and white the two signature colors of the blessed country are the main theme and conversational corners like the bakery,street signs and tasteful artfacts create a warm atmosphere exactly what Greeks are.Warm and hospitable.\nThe menu is so authentic and versatile using the Greek names of the dishes which is an educational experience and smartly done so that can bring you closer to the Greek culture.It a 3 floors split level establishment and every floor has a story to tell.A nice veranda offers an alfresco dining experience and iconography of saints on the top floor brings warmth to a living room alike chill out/dine area.\n\"Kouzina\"alias kitchen is a place to meet with friends,relax after an exhausting exploration of the city.Tender succulent pieces of meat grilled just right combined with tsatziki sauce and condiments fulfilled my cravings as I indulged in souvlaki.The tirokafteri and melitzanosalata\n dips were exploding in flavor...the finale a first class double shot cappuccino where I could even tell that the coffeeused was of premium standard.\nThe service is courteous and the manager explains the dishes while you order and when the order arrives.Very engaging as this is in the blood of Greeks.\nThere is a good mix of patrons .Foreigners living in Danang.visitors and tourists lovers of Greek food and Vietnamese.A well priced menu.\nRead more\nWritten February 2, 2020",
            "rating": 5.0,
